From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: xiaomi-lithium: enable the SLPI (sensors)

All of lithium's sensors sit behind the SLPI. Enable it with the stock
supplies: vdd_px from PM8994 LVS2 (stock qcom,ssc@1c00000 vdd_px-supply,
fed from S4 as on the other Xiaomi MSM8996 boards), vdd_cx through the
SLPI power domain. Firmware: the slpi_a4 build of the shared stock
NON-HLOS image, which lithium's stock DT names (qcom,msm-ssc-sensors).

With the in-kernel sensor registry given this phone's persist sns.reg
(firmware-xiaomi-lithium r2), the SLPI boots and the Sensor Manager
exposes accelerometer, gyroscope, magnetometer and pressure as IIO
devices; iio-sensor-proxy finds the accelerometer and Plasma Mobile's
auto-rotate follows the phone.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-lithium.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-lithium.dts
@@ -532,6 +532,8 @@
 	regulators-0 {
 		compatible = "qcom,rpm-pm8994-regulators";
 
+		vdd_lvs1_2-supply = <&vreg_s4a_1p8>;
+
 		/* Shared 1.8 V I/O rail; kept on, as on other MSM8996 boards. */
 		/* QCA6174 vdd-core (stock pm8994_s3, 1.3 V). */
 		vreg_s3a_1p3: s3 {
@@ -605,6 +607,13 @@
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-always-on;
 		};
+
+		/* SLPI vdd_px (stock pm8994 lvs2) */
+		vreg_lvs2a_1p8: lvs2 {
+			regulator-name = "vreg_lvs2a_1p8";
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		};
 	};
 };
 
@@ -803,6 +812,13 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&slpi_pil {
+	/* stock qcom,ssc@1c00000; lithium runs the slpi_a4 build of the shared firmware */
+	firmware-name = "qcom/msm8996/lithium/slpi.mbn";
+	px-supply = <&vreg_lvs2a_1p8>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &venus {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/msm8996/lithium/venus.mbn";
 	status = "okay";
